R03.summary:
I wrote the R03 (ear fan front) spec and its annotated image against assembled-0291. Both are committed by name on akinza/construction-loop (4e0b9dc8), with a plain message and no trailer. All measurements came from Python traces of the first sheet in the canonical() fit frame and from the head-0281 mesh.

The fan's outline already fits within about .01. The exceptions are the two tips, which end in flat vertical edges .030 to .036 tall where the sheet narrows to up-flared points at (.276, .033) and (-.273, .057), and the R lower edge, which sits up to .017 too high. The edge has 1 to 2 serrations per side against the sheet's 14 to 17. The cup is empty, where the sheet has a pale tuft (gray 180 against fur 99). The top band is a lip rolled .03 to .04 in front of the cup floor, which is why the fan reads as a dish and the V does not show. In profile the wing's front face hides the cup, where the sheet shows a tuft of area .0029 (gap audit rank 19).

The spec replaces the fan front with a construction, not a sculpt. Each side gets 10 primary edge locks with their tips on measured outline points (P1 to P8 large, P9 and P10 short drape locks), 9 fill locks behind them in the notches, 5 cup-rim locks over their roots, and 5 pale tuft locks rooted on the model's skull side line (|x| .100). They sit on an inset body plate. One table gives every lock's root, tip, length, widths, thickness, direction and front depth, in the model frame with head-local conversions. The spec also sets:
- a cup polygon with a clean rim and a pointed upper tip;
- a depth plan that moves the top band and outer wing back .017 to .048 and opens the cup sideways;
- a pale material (base value .58) for the tuft faces.

2D checks of the structure against the sheet predict:
- front fan missing .038 and extra .010, so R03.2 comes out about .049 against its .06 limit;
- ear span about 1.01;
- 12 and 14 serrations;
- the tuft covering .62 and .58 of the cup;
- a simulated side view showing a visible tuft of .0025 and .0023.

The must-not section gives the geometric cause of each failed look in the fan's build chain (crinkle, thorns, flat leaf plane, empty hollow, rolled lip, knobs and scales, square tip). Every audit row is marked structural except the tip trim, which is a local outline fix.

Six points of friction are flagged:
1. The model's face is wider than the sheet's (skull side .100 against .080 to .087), which costs about .015 of cup width per side.
2. The sheet itself measures .37 to .48 tuft coverage, so "at least half" is stricter than the reference.
3. A pale tuft needs a second material in the clay render.
4. Rank 19 has no criterion; the spec proposes one.
5. R03.3's V wording holds only on the L side.
6. The depth plan shares the wing volume with R04.
